Package: rhodep-aireplay-settle
Version: 2
Architecture: arm64
Maintainer: rhodep port
Priority: optional
Section: net
Depends: aircrack-ng, iw
Description: Wrap aireplay-ng with an iw set-channel + settle before exec
 WCN3990 firmware serializes monitor RX frames through a single mgmt-forwarder
 upcall that occasionally goes quiet after a chanctx transition (e.g. after
 airodump-ng started, after any iw set channel). External adapters like the
 TP-Link RTL8812AU do NOT have this bug because they push raw RX at hardware
 level to every PF_PACKET listener independently. There is no ath10k mainline
 WMI command to re-arm the fw forwarder; two attempts to patch this driver-
 side both crashed the firmware at cmnos_thread.c:4005 (see kernel/ath10k-
 rhodep-port/docs/5ghz-mgmt-forwarder-bug.md).
 .
 This package installs /usr/local/sbin/aireplay-ng as a wrapper that:
   1. Parses the target BSSID / channel from argv (or the fixed channel of
      wlan0mon if -c/--channel is absent).
   2. Runs `iw dev <iface> set channel <N>` explicitly to force the fw to
      re-run its chanctx transition.
   3. Sleeps 2 s so the fw mgmt-forwarder settles before aireplay-ng's
      wait_for_beacon loop starts.
   4. exec's the real /usr/bin/aireplay-ng with the original argv.
 .
 Once installed and with /usr/local/sbin in PATH ahead of /usr/bin (which
 systemd, sudo and Kali's default PATH already do), the natural
 airodump-ng + aireplay-ng two-window workflow works on the internal
 WCN3990 radio the same way it does on TP-Link adapters.
